t-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6\">\n      <span class=\"text-text-primary\">Security</span>\n      <span class=\"text-navy\">Insights</span>\n    </h1>\n    <p class=\"text-lg text-text-secondary max-w-3xl mx-auto\">\n      Technical deep-dives, industry analysis, and practical security guidance from the Cyberian Defenses team.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- Blog Posts -->\n<section class=\"py-20 px-6 lg:px-8\">\n  <div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <div class=\"space-y-6\" id=\"blog-posts-container\">\n      <!-- Posts injected via JavaScript -->\n      <div class=\"text-center py-10\">\n        <p class=\"text-text-secondary\">Loading articles...</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Pagination Controls -->\n    <div id=\"pagination-controls\" class=\"hidden\">\n      <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-border\">\n        <div id=\"pagination-prev\">\n          <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-text-secondary hover:text-navy transition-colors\">Previous</a>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"flex items-center gap-1\" id=\"pagination-pages\"></div>\n        <div id=\"pagination-next\">\n          <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-text-secondary hover:text-navy transition-colors\">Next</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"text-center text-sm text-text-muted mt-2\" id=\"pagination-summary\">\n        Page 1 of 1 (3 posts total)\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- CTA -->\n<section class=\"py-20 px-6 lg:px-8 bg-surface border-y border-border\">\n  <div class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center\">\n    <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Stay informed</h2>\n    <p class=\"text-text-secondary mb-8\">We publish in-depth security research and practical guides. Connect with us for updates.</p>\n    <a href=\"/contact.html\" class=\"inline-block bg-navy text-white px-8 py-3 text-sm font-semibold hover:brightness-110 transition-all\">Get in touch</a>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<script>\n// Blog data - sorted by date (newest first)\nconst blogPosts = [\n\n  {\n    title: 'AI-Assisted SharePoint RCE: What CVE-2026-55040 Means for Vulnerability Research Velocity',\n    date: '2026-08-17',\n    excerpt: 'Rapid7 used a heavily prompted AI agent to compress the discovery of an unauthenticated RCE chain in Microsoft SharePoint Server into 24 active days. CVE-2026-55040 (CVSS 9.1) is a JWT validation bypass chained to CVE-2026-63520 to run code as the site service account. The economics of zero-day discovery just shifted.',\n    url: '/blog/2026-08-17-ai-assisted-sharepoint-rce-cve-2026-55040',\n    tags: ['AI Security', 'CVE', 'Vulnerability Research']\n  },\n\n  {\n    title: 'Cross-Provider AI Reasoning Leakage: When Encrypted Thought Traces Become Attack Surface',\n    date: '2026-08-15',\n    excerpt: 'OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google encrypt the reasoning traces their models produce between API calls. Researchers recovered API keys, passwords, and internal model reasoning from those traces without breaking the encryption. The cross-provider portability means the exposure travels with your architecture decisions, not your vendor choice.',\n    url: '/blog/cross-provider-ai-reasoning-leakage',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY', 'LLM SECURITY', 'VULNERABILITY ANALYSIS']\n  },\n\n  {\n    title: 'Direct Prompt Injection in RAG and Agent Pipelines',\n    date: '2026-06-19',\n    excerpt: 'Poisoned documents in your vector store can silently rewrite system instructions and hijack agent tool calls. Flowise CVEs (CVSS 9.8), Bing Chat, and Copilot prove this is not theoretical \u2014 your RAG pipeline is one malicious document away from compromise.',\n    url: '/blog/direct-prompt-injection-rag-agent-pipelines',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY', 'LLM SECURITY', 'AGENT SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'JetBrains Marketplace Malicious Plugins: API Key Theft at Scale',\n    date: '2026-06-19',\n    excerpt: '15 malicious JetBrains plugins stole API keys, tokens, and credentials from 7 vendor accounts with ~70K downloads. Aikido Security traced the campaign to IP 39.107.60.51 \u2014 active from October 2025 through June 2026.',\n    url: '/blog/jetbrains-marketplace-api-key-theft',\n    tags: ['SUPPLY CHAIN', 'API SECURITY', 'THREAT INTEL']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'When Distillation Becomes Espionage: The US House Recommendation and What It Means for AI Security',\n    date: '2026-06-12',\n    excerpt: 'The US House Select Committee on China recommended treating model extraction as industrial espionage under the Economic Espionage Act. Google disclosed 100,000+ extraction prompts against Gemini. Anthropic flagged 16M extraction exchanges. The direction of travel is unambiguous.',\n    url: '/blog/distillation-as-espionage',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY', 'LLM SECURITY', 'LEGAL']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Your SOC Analysts Deserve to Know Why: NLLog and Explainable Anomaly Detection',\n    date: '2026-06-04',\n    excerpt: 'NLLog rewrites parsed log templates into WHO-WHAT-SEVERITY natural language sentences before applying anomaly detection \u2014 a lightweight pipeline that optimizes for understandability, not just recall. 99.3% precision on HDFS, TreeSHAP explainability, commodity hardware.',\n    url: '/blog/nllog-explainable-soc-anomaly-detection',\n    tags: ['AI Security', 'SOC', 'Anomaly Detection']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'AgentRedBench: Why Your LLM Agent Pipeline Leaks Through Every SaaS Integration',\n    date: '2026-06-02',\n    excerpt: 'AgentRedBench tests 215 indirect prompt injection scenarios across 24 SaaS integrations using 8 frontier models. No-guard ASR: 32% (Claude) to 81% (Gemini). AgentRedGuard cuts ASR to 2.4% at 0.37% FPR.',\n    url: '/blog/agentredbench-llm-agent-redteaming',\n    tags: ['AgentRedBench', 'LLM Security', 'Prompt Injection']\n  },  {\n    title: 'EU AI Act Conformit\u00e9 pour Syst\u00e8mes d\\'IA \u00e0 Haut Risque',\n    date: '2026-06-01',\n    excerpt: 'L\\'\u00e9valuation de conformit\u00e9 au titre du r\u00e8glement IA n\\'est pas une checklist administrative \u2014 c\\'est un audit technique dont la responsabilit\u00e9 incombe au d\u00e9ployeur, pas \u00e0 l\\'\u00e9diteur. Article 15, article 29, article 99 \u2014 dates, p\u00e9nalit\u00e9s, obligations',\n    url: '/blog/eu-ai-act-conformite-systemes-haut-risque',\n    tags: ['EU AI ACT', 'CONFORMIT\u00c9', 'R\u00c9GLEMENTATION']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'HuggingFace Model Hub Typosquatting and Malicious Weights',\n    date: '2026-06-01',\n    excerpt: 'Typosquatting attacks on HuggingFace model repositories exploit trust in pretrained weights \u2014 CVE-2026-2651 (CVSS 9.0) enables artifact overwriting in MLflow, and new research shows LoRA adapter backdoors that pass eval benchmarks but flip outputs on',\n    url: '/blog/huggingface-model-hub-typosquatting-malicious-weights',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY', 'LLM SECURITY', 'SUPPLY CHAIN']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Langflow CVE-2025-34291 \u2014 Iranian APT MuddyWater Actively Exploiting AI Orchestration',\n    date: '2026-05-26',\n    excerpt: 'CVE-2025-34291 (CVSS 9.4) \u2014 origin validation RCE in Langflow actively exploited by Iranian state-sponsored MuddyWater. CISA KEV confirmed May 21, 2026. Unauthenticated remote code execution with credential exfiltration.',\n    url: '/blog/langflow-cve-2025-34291-muddywater',\n    tags: ['CVE ANALYSIS', 'AI SECURITY', 'APT', 'IRAN', 'LANGFLOW', 'MUDDYWATER']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'CVE-2026-26980 \u2014 AI-Discovered SQL Injection in Ghost CMS | Cyberian Defenses',\n    date: '2026-05-26',\n    excerpt: 'Technical deep-dive into CVE-2026-26980: unauthenticated SQL injection discovered via Claude/Glasswing, exploited via ClickFix malware delivery.',\n    url: '/blog/ghost-cms-cve-2026-26980-ai-discovery-clickfix',\n    tags: ['CYBERSECURITY', 'PENETRATION TESTING', 'AI SECURITY', 'ISO 27001', 'COMPLIANCE', 'MENA', 'TUNISIA', 'AFRICA']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'WolfSSL CVE-2026-5194: The Structural Speed Gap Between AI Discovery and Human Patch Cycles',\n    date: '2026-05-26',\n    excerpt: 'WolfSSL certificate forgery vulnerability (CVSS 9.1) discovered by Claude Mythos Preview. Structural analysis: AI finds 82 vulnerabilities per day while embedded patch cycles run 30-90 days minimum.',\n    url: '/blog/wolfssl-cve-2026-5194-glasswing',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY', 'CVE ANALYSIS']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Supply Chain Under Siege: Zero-Click WolfSSL Compromise in Glasswing AI Deployments',\n    date: '2026-05-25',\n    excerpt: 'CVE-2026-5194 is a zero-click remote code execution vulnerability in WolfSSL used by Glasswing AI deployments. The flaw enables supply chain compromise through malicious TLS library updates \u2014 no user interaction required. Full analysis of the attack ',\n    url: '/blog/wolfssl-glasswing-supply-chain-cve-2026-5194',\n    tags: ['CVE ANALYSIS', 'SUPPLY CHAIN', 'VULNERABILITY RESEARCH']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Vulnerability Mechanics: Two Critical Flaws, One Root Cause',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'On May 29, 2026, two critical vulnerabilities were disclosed in SillyTavern, an open-source LLM frontend used for interacting with text generation models, image...',\n    url: '/blog/sillytavern-cve-2026-44649-44650',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'LLM-Powered Automated Vulnerability Discovery: What the Research Actually Shows',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Claude Mythos found thousands of high-severity flaws across every major OS and browser. Three new papers from May 2026 explain why defense won\\'t catch up easily. Detection rules and mitigations for the discovery-validation gap.',\n    url: '/blog/llm-powered-automated-vulnerability-discovery',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'The Problem',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Every LLM agent platform shipping today adds persistent memory. The pitch is personalization: the agent remembers your preferences, your priorities, your commun...',\n    url: '/blog/memory-induced-tool-drift-llm-agents',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'CVE-2026-41863: Spring AI Anthropic Skills API Path Traversal',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Technical deep-dive into CVE-2026-41863 \u2014 LLM-influenced filenames in Spring AI\\'s Anthropic Skills API lead to path traversal via Path.resolve(). CVSS 6.5. Detection, mitigation, and attack scenarios.',\n    url: '/blog/spring-ai-cve-2026-41863-path-traversal',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'NIS2 et services d\\'IA : ce que les fournisseurs doivent int\u00e9grer maintenant',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'La directive NIS2 (UE) 2022/2555 impose aux fournisseurs de services d\\'IA une notification sous 24 heures, sous peine de sanctions jusqu\\'\u00e0 10 M\u20ac. Analyse compl\u00e8te des obligations, sanctions, d\u00e9lais et mesures op\u00e9rationnelles.',\n    url: '/blog/nis2-directive-implications-services-ia',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Three Critical RCEs in SGLang \u2014 No Patch Available',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Technical deep-dive into CVE-2026-7301, CVE-2026-7302, CVE-2026-7304 in SGLang. pickle/dill deserialization RCEs. No patch. Network segmentation only mitigation.',\n    url: '/blog/sglang-triple-critical-rce-no-patch-cve-2026-7301-7302-7304',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'SGLang Triple Critical RCE: No Patch, Three Attack Vectors, One Infrastructure Problem',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'CVE-2026-7301 (CVSS 9.8) | CVE-2026-7302 (CVSS 9.1) | CVE-2026-7304 (CVSS 9.8) CERT-CC VU#777338 | Published May 15, 2026 Vendor: SGLang / sgl-project on GitHub...',\n    url: '/blog/sglang-triple-critical-rce-cve-2026-7301-7302-7304',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Vulnerability Overview',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'CVE-2026-10105 is a SQL injection vulnerability in agno 2.6.5, an open-source AI agent orchestration framework. The flaw lives in the ClickHouse vector database...',\n    url: '/blog/agno-cve-2026-10105-clickhouse-sql-injection',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Model Extraction Attacks via Repeated API Queries: The Cost Question Nobody Asks',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Carlini et al. showed in 2024 that a production LLM\\'s embedding layer and attention head count can be reconstructed from fewer than 10,000 API queries. Two years later, systematic extraction campaigns are observed in the wild. What is the annualized',\n    url: '/blog/model-extraction-attacks-api-queries',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'ChatGPhish: ChatGPT Web Summaries as a Phishing Surface',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'How ChatGPT\\'s web summary feature leaks organizational metadata through automatic resource fetching \u2014 technical analysis and mitigation steps.',\n    url: '/blog/chatgphish-chatgpt-web-summaries-phishing-surface',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Securing LLM Deployments Against Prompt Injection | Cyberian Defenses',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Technical guide: defending enterprise LLM deployments from prompt injection attacks. Practical strategies for AI security practitioners.',\n    url: '/blog/securing-llm-deployments',\n    tags: ['CYBERSECURITY', 'PENETRATION TESTING', 'AI SECURITY', 'ISO 27001', 'COMPLIANCE', 'MENA', 'TUNISIA', 'AFRICA']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Agents Need Boundaries, Not Just Prompts',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Agents have agency: they adapt and find multiple ways to solve problems. This autonomy creates a fundamental security challenge \u2014 the LLM at the heart of the ag...',\n    url: '/blog/aws-bedrock-agentcore-cedar-policy',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'How Tool Description Poisoning Works',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'ArXiv paper 2605.24069 (Liu et al., May 2026) introduces Tool Description Poisoning (TDP), a semantic attack class targeting the Model Context Protocol (MCP). U...',\n    url: '/blog/mcp-poisoning-llm-agent-attacks',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'GPU Isolation Failures in Multi-Tenant AI Clusters: The Shared Memory Problem Nobody Audits',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Multi-tenant Kubernetes clusters share GPU memory, PCIe buses, and NVLink fabrics across pods. The container runtime isolates filesystem and process namespace \u2014 but not the GPU\\'s memory bus. Research in 2025-2026 demonstrates timing side channels an',\n    url: '/blog/gpu-isolation-failures-multi-tenant-clusters',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Trojan Backdoors in Agent Harnesses: From Prompt Injection to Persistent Control | Cyberian Defenses',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'ClawTrojan achieves 95.5% attack success rate on GPT-5.4 via multi-step trojan backdoors planted through file system persistence \u2014 not prompt injection at runtime.',\n    url: '/blog/trojan-backdoors-agent-harnesses',\n    tags: ['CLAWTROJAN', 'DASGUARD', 'TROJAN BACKDOOR', 'AGENT HARNESS', 'PROMPT INJECTION', 'AI SECURITY', 'AGENT SECURITY', 'SUPPLY CHAIN SECURITY', 'LLM AGENT', 'PERSISTENT CONTROL']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'How Prompt Overflow Bypasses Guardrails',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'ArXiv paper 2605.23196 (Zhou et al., May 2026) identifies a structural blind spot: guardrail models use shorter context windows than the LLMs they protect, and ...',\n    url: '/blog/prompt-overflow-guardrail-bypass',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Gradient-Based Adversarial Attacks on Deep Neural Networks | Cyberian Defenses',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'How gradient-based adversarial attacks (FGSM, PGD, C&W) break production models \u2014 with code, CVE data, and 6 actionable CISO recommendations.',\n    url: '/blog/gradient-based-adversarial-attacks',\n    tags: ['ADVERSARIAL MACHINE LEARNING', 'FGSM', 'PGD', 'C&W', 'GRADIENT ATTACKS', 'AI SECURITY', 'ML SECURITY', 'ADVERSARIAL EXAMPLES']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Introduction: The Hidden Variable in Autonomous Red Teaming',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'When a red team runs an autonomous LLM penetration test, the standard workflow is: pick a model, write a prompt, let it attack, read the output. If it finds som...',\n    url: '/blog/llm-pentest-consistency-400-run-study-erdem-2026',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'ChatGPhish: ChatGPT\\'s Web Summary Feature as a Reconnaissance Vector',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Disclosed by: Permiso Security (May 2026) Source: The Hacker News Type: Design behavior exploitation \u2014 no CVE, no patch',\n    url: '/blog/chatgphish-chatgpt-reconnaissance-vector',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'First Real-World LLM Agent Attack \u2014 Marimo CVE-2026-39987',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Sysdig reports the first confirmed real threat actor weaponizing an LLM agent in a live breach chain. CVE-2026-39987, IoCs, detection engineering, and defensive guidance.',\n    url: '/blog/first-real-world-llm-agent-attack-marimo-cve-2026-39987',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'The Problem with Current Jailbreak Taxonomies',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Existing jailbreak attacks fall into two broad categories:',\n    url: '/blog/bait-jailbreak-llm-self-conditioned-reasoning',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'The First Real-World LLM Agent Attack Chain: What the Marimo Breach Means for AI Security',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Source: Sysdig Threat Research Team / The Hacker News, May 2026 CVE: CVE-2026-39987 \u2014 CVSS 9.8 (Critical) Vector: CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H I...',\n    url: '/blog/marimo-llm-agent-attack-chain-cve-2026-39987',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Side-Channel Attacks on Neural Network Inference: The Physical Layer Your Threat Model Misses',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Encryption protects model weights at rest and in transit. It does nothing during inference. Side-channel attacks \u2014 timing, cache behavior, power draw, electromagnetic emission \u2014 bypass all access controls because they exploit the physical properties ',\n    url: '/blog/side-channel-attacks-neural-network-inference',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Black-Box Adversarial Attacks via Query Optimization | Cyberian Defenses',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Black-box adversarial attacks via query optimization \u2014 the production API threat model. ZOO, SimBA, HopSkipJump, and the practical attack chain at under 200 queries.',\n    url: '/blog/black-box-adversarial-query-optimization',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'System Prompt Leakage from Deployed LLMs: What the 1% Measurement Means for Your Guardrails',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Zhang et al. (USENIX Security 2026) measured ~200,000 real-world resumes from hireEZ and found roughly 1% contained prompt injection attempts targeting system instructions. This is the first systematic measurement of prompt injection in a live LLM de',\n    url: '/blog/system-prompt-leakage-deployed-llms',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'CVE-2026-7301: SGLang Router Unauthenticated RCE',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Technical deep-dive into CVE-2026-7301 \u2014 SGLang\\'s ZeroMQ router deserializes pickle on 0.0.0.0. CVSS 9.8. Detection, mitigation, and attack chain.',\n    url: '/blog/sglang-cve-2026-7301-router-unauthenticated-rce',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Data Poisoning in Web-Scale Training Pipelines',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Two independent disclosures this week confirm the same blind spot in ML pipelines: artifact integrity. CVE-2026-2651 (MLflow, CVSS 9.0) and CVE-2026-8596/8597 (AWS SageMaker) \u2014 same root cause, two vendors. Plus research from arXiv:2605.30189 and arX',\n    url: '/blog/data-poisoning-web-scale-training-pipelines',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  },\n  {\n    title: 'Introduction',\n    date: '2025-01-01',\n    excerpt: 'Most organizations deploying AI agents today treat security testing as an LLM problem. They test for prompt injection, jailbreaks, and output alignment. What th...',\n    url: '/blog/ibm-pentests-agent-systems-eykholt-2025',\n    tags: ['AI SECURITY']\n  }\n];\n\n// Configuration\nconst postsPerPage = 10;\n\n// Parse URL query params\nfunction getUrlParams() {\n  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\n  let page = parseInt(params.get('page')) || 1;\n  if (isNaN(page) || page < 1) page = 1;\n  return { page };\n}\n\n// Render posts for current page\nfunction renderPosts() {\n  const { page } = getUrlParams();\n  const totalPages = Math.ceil(blogPosts.length / postsPerPage);\n  const start = (page - 1) * postsPerPage;\n  const currentPosts = blogPosts.slice(start, start + postsPerPage);\n\n  const container = document.getElementById('blog-posts-container');\n\n  if (currentPosts.length === 0) {\n    container.innerHTML = '<div class=\"text-center py-10\"><p class=\"text-text-secondary\">No articles found.</p></div>';\n    return;\n  }\n\n  container.innerHTML = currentPosts.map(post => `\n    <article class=\"bg-surface border border-border p-6\">\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4\">\n        <span class=\"font-mono text-xs text-navy bg-navy-dim px-2 py-0.5\">${post.tags.join(' ')}</span>\n        <span class=\"font-mono text-xs text-text-muted\">${post.date}</span>\n      </div>\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-3\">\n        <a href=\"${post.url}\" class=\"text-text-primary hover:text-navy transition-colors\">\n          ${post.title}\n        </a>\n      </h2>\n      <p class=\"text-text-secondary mb-4\">\n        ${post.excerpt}\n      </p>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n        <span class=\"text-text-secondary text-sm\">By Ahmed Chiboub</span>\n        <a href=\"${post.url}\" class=\"text-navy hover:text-text-primary transition-colors text-sm font-semibold\">\n          Read More\n        </a>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  `).join('\\n');\n\n  // Show pagination only if more than 10 posts\n  if (blogPosts.length > 10) {\n    renderPagination(page, totalPages);\n  }\n}\n\n// Render pagination controls\nfunction renderPagination(currentPage, totalPages) {\n  const controls = document.getElementById('pagination-controls');\n  controls.classList.remove('hidden');\n\n  // Update summary\n  document.getElementById('pagination-summary').textContent = `Page ${currentPage} of ${totalPages} (${blogPosts.length} posts total)`;\n\n  // Generate page links\n  const pagesContainer = document.getElementById('pagination-pages');\n  let pageLinks = '';\n\n  // Calculate page numbers to show (max 5 pages visible)\n  let startPage = Math.max(1, currentPage - 2);\n  let endPage = Math.min(totalPages, startPage + 4);\n  if (endPage - startPage < 4) {\n    startPage = Math.max(1, endPage - 4);\n  }\n\n  for (let p = startPage; p <= endPage; p++) {\n    if (p === currentPage) {\n      pageLinks += `<span class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 font-semibold text-text-primary\">${p}</span>`;\n    } else {\n      const url = p === 1 ? '/blog' : `/blog?page=${p}`;\n      pageLinks += `<a href=\"${url}\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 font-semibold text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary transition-colors\">${p}</a>`;\n    }\n  }\n  pagesContainer.innerHTML = pageLinks;\n\n  // Previous/Next buttons\n  const prevBtn = document.getElementById('pagination-prev');\n  const nextBtn = document.getElementById('pagination-next');\n\n  if (currentPage > 1) {\n    prevBtn.innerHTML = `<a href=\"/blog?page=${currentPage - 1}\" class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-text-secondary hover:text-navy transition-colors\">Previous</a>`;\n    prevBtn.classList.remove('hidden');\n  } else {\n    prevBtn.classList.add('hidden');\n  }\n\n  if (currentPage < totalPages) {\n    nextBtn.innerHTML = `<a href=\"/blog?page=${currentPage + 1}\" class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-text-secondary hover:text-navy transition-colors\">Next</a>`;\n    nextBtn.classList.remove('hidden');\n  } else {\n    nextBtn.classList.add('hidden');\n  }\n}\n\n// Initial render\nrenderPosts();\n</script>\n<!-- Footer -->\n<footer class=\"border-t border-border py-10 px-6 lg:px-8 bg-surface\">\n    <div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-4\">\n        <div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-text-secondary font-mono\">\n            <span class=\"text-text-primary font-sans font-semibold\">Cyberian Defenses</span>\n            <span class=\"text-border\">|</span>\n            <span>Tunis \u00b7 MENA \u00b7 Africa</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"flex gap-6 text-sm text-text-secondary\">\n            <a href=\"https://linkedin.com/in/ahmed-chiboub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"hover:text-navy transition-colors\">LinkedIn</a>\n            <a href=\"https://github.com/cybathreat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"hover:text-navy transition-colors\">GitHub</a>\n            <a href=\"mailto:ahmed.chiboub@cyberian-defenses.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"hover:text-navy transition-colors\">Email</a>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</footer>\n</body>\n</html>", "stderr": "", "duration_sec": 0.15, "success": true}}